  o Minor bugfixes (OOM handler):
    - Treat a buffer that holds no data as having age zero, and otherwise
      use the age of its first chunk that holds data. Previously, a drained
      buffer could keep an empty chunk left over from an earlier read, and
      its reported age kept growing while the connection sat idle. Under
      memory pressure, this made us close idle connections (and circuits
      with idle streams) before ones with genuinely old queued data,
      freeing almost no memory. Bugfix on 0.2.5.3-alpha.
